  "title": "# Build: md-studio (Urgent profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): build MD Studio.",
  "asked": "# Build: md-studio (Urgent profile) Brett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): build MD Studio. It was planned but NEVER built (no branch, no log). Assigned agent: **Reel Rhonda** (book on her agent-swarm card; set AXF_AGENT=reel-rhonda if supported, else record in report + store note). ## First - s0 Search the hub memory/notes (`/projects/_shared/_claude/notes/`, `/projects/amberx-axf/_claude/`, THREADS, store, plans/) and GitHub for any MD Studio plan/spec Brett wrote; that spec wins over this brief. Register in Urgent (id `md-studio`), banner entry. ## Build (unless his spec says otherwise) - MD Studio = a Markdown studio plugin for the Dev Console built ON the dock engine (molly-fable #245, now on main): dockable panes for file tree, editor, live preview, outline. - Editor with markdown toolbar (headings, bold/italic, lists, checklists, tables, code, links), live preview side by side or split, tabs for multiple docs, search/replace, autosave, version history with restore. - **Notes section step (required):** a Notes section that opens and edits everything in the Notes Vault (`/projects/_shared/_claude/notes/` incl. sessions/, handoffs/, plans/, install/, misc/, INDEX.md) using the Notes Vault commands that landed with plugin-commands-auto; plus opening hub memory/rules files and repo .md files. - Every command declared once so REST + MCP + CLI are generated (standing rule), so Amber can open/edit docs by voice. - Tokens/theme only for styling; works on phone (compact window class) first. - Tests, report `_claude/builds/reports/md-studio.md`, THREADS, PR, mark steps done through the store. Commits clean and professional. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches (Brett, Nov 3 2026): a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. An UPGRADE (e.g. Opus → Fable) needs Brett's approval: when you reach one, run `node apps/console-web/plugins/build-orchestrator/orchestrator.mjs request-upgrade <id> <phase>`, ask once, and stop. Never approve a model switch upgrade yourself (no `act approve` on an upgrade), never relaunch on a higher model.",
